1
00:00:04,449 --> 00:00:06,269
My cat just fought my landlord.

2
00:00:06,269 --> 00:00:06,799
I'm Mara.

3
00:00:06,799 --> 00:00:09,749
I have two minutes, and
I'm locked in with myself.

4
00:00:10,482 --> 00:00:11,542
She locked me in.

5
00:00:11,542 --> 00:00:13,152
Then she told me why.

6
00:00:13,352 --> 00:00:15,002
One word. Lie.

7
00:00:15,412 --> 00:00:16,372
Mister Crane lied?

8
00:00:16,372 --> 00:00:17,022
I'm shocked.

9
00:00:17,022 --> 00:00:17,182
No.

10
00:00:17,182 --> 00:00:17,712
I'm lying.

11
00:00:17,712 --> 00:00:18,872
I'm not shocked.

12
00:00:19,072 --> 00:00:21,122
She had tried his trade already.

13
00:00:21,122 --> 00:00:21,832
Last night.

14
00:00:21,832 --> 00:00:22,902
My tomorrow.

15
00:00:23,202 --> 00:00:24,882
She gave herself up for Mom.

16
00:00:24,882 --> 00:00:26,512
And he kept them both.

17
00:00:27,102 --> 00:00:29,832
It's eleven fifty
nine, Miss Reyes.

18
00:00:29,932 --> 00:00:31,572
Zip, get behind me.

19
00:00:31,672 --> 00:00:33,122
No. I was a bouncer.

20
00:00:33,322 --> 00:00:35,282
What is that cat doing?

21
00:00:35,482 --> 00:00:36,732
You're not on the list!

22
00:00:37,432 --> 00:00:40,452
He burned so bright that
Crane covered his eyes.

23
00:00:40,652 --> 00:00:41,722
The door was open.

24
00:00:41,722 --> 00:00:43,862
And only one of us could leave.

25
00:00:44,062 --> 00:00:45,292
So I picked.

26
00:00:46,092 --> 00:00:47,442
Mara! No! Mara!

27
00:00:48,242 --> 00:00:49,712
I tried to say goodbye.

28
00:00:49,712 --> 00:00:51,162
No sound came out.

29
00:00:52,716 --> 00:00:54,856
Now I'm the one
sending messages.

30
00:00:55,056 --> 00:00:56,786
Inside nine, you can't speak.

31
00:00:56,786 --> 00:00:58,226
You can only bend glass.

32
00:00:58,226 --> 00:00:59,896
And the glass runs out.

33
00:01:00,206 --> 00:01:02,446
Through the wall, I
could see my shop.

34
00:01:02,446 --> 00:01:03,086
Last night.

35
00:01:03,086 --> 00:01:05,036
And me, not knowing a thing.

36
00:01:05,236 --> 00:01:05,926
I needed her.

37
00:01:05,926 --> 00:01:07,496
But I would have to ask.

38
00:01:07,696 --> 00:01:10,536
I have never asked anyone
for help in my life.

39
00:01:11,136 --> 00:01:12,446
So I wrote it.

40
00:01:13,746 --> 00:01:15,096
It says hello! It's friendly.

41
00:01:15,096 --> 00:01:15,856
I love it.

42
00:01:16,056 --> 00:01:18,716
I had forgotten how
much I love that idiot.

43
00:01:19,226 --> 00:01:20,276
I wrote tomorrow.

44
00:01:20,276 --> 00:01:21,076
I wrote nine.

45
00:01:21,076 --> 00:01:22,616
I wrote, don't turn.

46
00:01:23,006 --> 00:01:23,896
And she turned.

47
00:01:23,896 --> 00:01:25,146
Of course she turned.

48
00:01:25,146 --> 00:01:25,796
I did.

49
00:01:26,306 --> 00:01:28,786
Every one of you asks
yourself for help.

50
00:01:28,786 --> 00:01:31,126
And every one of
you comes alone.

51
00:01:31,716 --> 00:01:34,116
Then a word lit up
that I did not write.

52
00:01:34,916 --> 00:01:36,776
Here. In my mother's hand.

53
00:01:37,686 --> 00:01:39,476
And I had one tube left.

54
00:01:41,032 --> 00:01:43,492
I could write any
word, except that one.

55
00:01:43,702 --> 00:01:45,062
Help was always to me.

56
00:01:45,062 --> 00:01:46,852
And I always came alone.

57
00:01:47,052 --> 00:01:49,632
So I bent my last
tube into one letter.

58
00:01:50,232 --> 00:01:52,632
And through the wall,
my mother bent hers.

59
00:01:53,222 --> 00:01:54,092
Us.

60
00:01:54,992 --> 00:01:56,702
And the whole street answered.

61
00:01:58,002 --> 00:02:00,362
Stop that! You'll
break the ring!

62
00:02:00,362 --> 00:02:02,482
Sir, I'm going to have
to ask you to leave.

63
00:02:02,682 --> 00:02:05,882
Fool! Break the ring,
and they all go out!

64
00:02:05,982 --> 00:02:07,982
Out. Yes. That's the idea.

65
00:02:09,182 --> 00:02:10,422
And out they came.

66
00:02:10,422 --> 00:02:10,772
Ruth.

67
00:02:10,772 --> 00:02:11,122
Otis.

68
00:02:11,122 --> 00:02:13,772
Pete, still asking
about his oven.

69
00:02:14,162 --> 00:02:15,672
The other me took my hand.

70
00:02:15,672 --> 00:02:17,552
And then there was just me.

71
00:02:18,752 --> 00:02:20,082
Mara?

72
00:02:20,382 --> 00:02:21,352
Mom.

73
00:02:21,962 --> 00:02:23,752
Look how tall you are.

74
00:02:23,842 --> 00:02:25,282
You left your coat.

75
00:02:25,982 --> 00:02:28,122
I'm not crying.
I'm leaking argon.

76
00:02:28,632 --> 00:02:31,962
By morning, every light on
the street was just a light.

77
00:02:32,262 --> 00:02:32,512
Mara?

78
00:02:32,512 --> 00:02:34,382
When did we get a number eleven?

79
00:02:34,782 --> 00:02:36,282
And somebody knocked.
